#N canvas 20 20 1900 900 12;
#X text 20 20 lp-poll-probe -- DOES [sysexin] FIRE ON THE ORGANELLE? Item 98 answered that on the Mac and nothing has ever tested it here \, and the whole replug fix rests on it. Loads as a third patch beside mother.pd and main.pd. Every 5 seconds it sends the universal device inquiry to MIDI port 1 and prints whatever comes back. It touches no bus in Cut It and owns no surface., f 120;
#X text 20 140 WHAT TO EXPECT. A reply is 17 bytes starting 240 126 0 6 2 and carrying 0 32 41 -- Novation. If PROBE-SYSEX prints those every five seconds the poll is viable on this platform. If it prints NOTHING while the device is plugged in \, [sysexin] does not work here and the replug fix needs a different detector., f 120;
#X text 20 260 THEN UNPLUG THE LAUNCHPAD. On the Mac the replies keep coming -- item 99b. ON THE DEVICE THEY SHOULD STOP AND NEVER COME BACK \, even after replugging \, because the ALSA subscription is destroyed and only wire.sh recreates it. That asymmetry is the whole reason the fix cannot be the same on both platforms \, and this probe is what proves it rather than assuming it., f 120;
#X obj 20 420 loadbang;
#X obj 20 470 del 4000;
#X obj 20 520 metro 5000;
#X msg 20 570 240 \, 126 \, 127 \, 6 \, 1 \, 247;
#X obj 20 620 s \$0-out;
#X obj 700 420 r \$0-out;
#X obj 700 570 midiout;
#X obj 1050 420 loadbang;
#X obj 1050 470 f 1;
#X text 1050 520 the port goes into the cold inlet at load -- u_init's proven pattern \, not a creation argument., f 44;
#X obj 1500 420 sysexin;
#X obj 1500 470 print PROBE-SYSEX;
#X obj 1500 570 midiin;
#X obj 1500 620 print PROBE-RAW;
#X text 1500 680 RAW-IN is the wider net: it fires for every incoming byte of any kind \, so if the device answers with anything at all this sees it even when sysexin does not., f 44;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 9 1;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
